    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (81.08) and **Yordan Alvarez** (80.06) headline the Zurich Zebras lineup as our most potent assets. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an elite matchup against Arrighetti, whose 4.97 xERA provides a soft landing; his elite speed profile is significantly boosted by the pitcher's slow delivery, making him a prime candidate for a stolen base. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in core play, as his xwOBA of 0.421 overrides the slight negative wind-in penalty, allowing his power profile to flourish against Taillon despite the park factors. **Dillon Dingler** (63.75) also commands attention; his dynamic platoon edge against the lefty Akin, combined with a premium spot in the #2 hole, cements his status as our primary backstop option.\n\nThe decision to keep **Chase Meidroth** (39.03) on the bench was the tightest call of the day, ultimately dictated by our strict 40.0 floor for daily efficiency. While **Chase Meidroth** offered some utility, he couldn\u2019t overcome the significant SP skill hurdle posed by McDonald. Elsewhere, we are exercising caution with **Junior Caminero** (55.47), whose score was suppressed by a daunting matchup against Cole. Despite being a high-ceiling talent, the combination of a zero-xERA opponent and unfavorable wind-in conditions makes him a marginal start. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Casey Schmitt** (57.89); while he projects as a strong play if confirmed in the #3 spot, we remain prepared to adjust if the final order shifts. Owners should note that **Trea Turner** (63.16) and **Kyle Schwarber** (60.32) are dealing with a wind-in warning at the stadium, which tempers their offensive ceiling slightly, though their high base projections keep them firmly in our starting rotation.",
